#: ../../source/extsprintf_README.md:1
msgid "extsprintf: extended POSIX-style sprintf"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/extsprintf_README.md:3
msgid ""
"Stripped down version of s[n]printf(3c).  We make a best effort to throw "
"an exception when given a format string we don't understand, rather than "
"ignoring it, so that we won't break existing programs if/when we go "
"implement the rest of this."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/extsprintf_README.md:8
msgid "This implementation currently supports specifying"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/extsprintf_README.md:10
msgid "field alignment ('-' flag),"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/extsprintf_README.md:11
msgid "zero-pad ('0' flag)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/extsprintf_README.md:12
msgid "always show numeric sign ('+' flag),"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/extsprintf_README.md:13
msgid "field width"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/extsprintf_README.md:14
msgid "conversions for strings, decimal integers, and floats (numbers)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/extsprintf_README.md:15
msgid ""
"argument size specifiers.  These are all accepted but ignored, since "
"Javascript has no notion of the physical size of an argument."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/extsprintf_README.md:18
msgid ""
"Everything else is currently unsupported, most notably: precision, "
"unsigned numbers, non-decimal numbers, and characters."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/extsprintf_README.md:21
msgid "Besides the usual POSIX conversions, this implementation supports:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/extsprintf_README.md:23
msgid "`%j`: pretty-print a JSON object (using node's \"inspect\")"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/extsprintf_README.md:24
#, python-format
msgid "`%r`: pretty-print an Error object"
msgstr ""

